From 4906697f965eff379949ef565d612b9782375c00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 12:22:54 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(memory): recall UX + import hardening (verify-panel
 round) (9c8060f8)

Verify-panel fixes on the memory->kernel+FTS5 consolidation:
- recall --json now returns an object {notes,total,capped,scope} so programmatic
  consumers can detect truncation (was a bare, silently-capped array).
- default `recall` (no query) is scoped to human `remember` notes and no longer
  miscounts; `--all` widens it to machine/insights records. --all is a GLOBAL
  boolean flag: read from the handler's flags arg (bin/forge.js sets flags.all)
  or the raw args on a direct call.
- insights/typed records render readably + LABELED with their source, never a
  raw JSON blob mislabeled as a plain note.
- query recall header signals top-N when capped ("Top N ... raise --limit").
- JSONL import: id-less records key off a content hash so a re-run / failed
  rename cannot double-insert.
- tests: --json object shape, capped header render, tag recall, --all widening,
  malformed/empty JSONL line tolerance. 93 memory+migration tests pass.

Blocker (FTS backfill-on-upgrade) fixed separately in 23bf9aa8.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
